      "content": "Hayek's concept of spontaneous order suggests that complex social arrangements, like the flow of information online, arise from decentralized individual actions rather than top-down planning. State interference, such as mandatory content moderation rules, acts as an artificial command, disrupting this natural, emergent process of idea discovery. When the government dictates what is \"allowed\" or \"disallowed,\" it replaces the complex, organic feedback of the digital public square with rigid, politically motivated constraints. This ultimately leads to an inefficient and distorted information ecosystem.",
